<p>Before diving into the philosophy, take a few minutes to explore the course website. This short activity will make sure you know how to find everything you need.</p>

<h2><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">&#127919;</span> Your Mission</h2>

<p>Complete each of the following tasks. There's nothing to submit — this is just to make sure you're comfortable navigating the site before we begin.</p>

<h2><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">&#9745;&#65039;</span> Checklist</h2>

<div class="callout callout--concept">
  <span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">1&#65039;&#8419;</span>
  <div class="callout__content">
    <p><strong>Explore the sidebar.</strong> Click on at least three different modules in the sidebar to expand them. Notice how each module contains a list of pages.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout callout--concept">
  <span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">2&#65039;&#8419;</span>
  <div class="callout__content">
    <p><strong>Navigate with tabs.</strong> Go to any unit page (try <a href="/phil1301/unit-1-socrates/introducing-philosophy/">Introducing Philosophy</a>) and click through each tab to see how lesson content is organized.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout callout--concept">
  <span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">3&#65039;&#8419;</span>
  <div class="callout__content">
    <p><strong>Use Previous and Next.</strong> Scroll to the bottom of any lesson page and use the navigation buttons to move forward and backward through the course.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout callout--concept">
  <span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">4&#65039;&#8419;</span>
  <div class="callout__content">
    <p><strong>Follow the breadcrumbs.</strong> Look at the small links at the top of any page (e.g., <em>Home &rsaquo; PHIL 1301 &rsaquo; Unit 1</em>). Click "PHIL 1301" to jump back to the course landing page.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout callout--concept">
  <span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">5&#65039;&#8419;</span>
  <div class="callout__content">
    <p><strong>Find your instructor.</strong> Navigate to the <a href="/phil1301/start-here/meet-your-instructor-2/">Meet Your Instructor</a> page and read through it.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout callout--concept">
  <span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">6&#65039;&#8419;</span>
  <div class="callout__content">
    <p><strong>Check the course overview.</strong> Go back to the <a href="/phil1301/">course landing page</a> and look at all eight module cards. Get a sense of the full journey ahead.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout callout--connection">
  <span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10145;&#65039;</span>
  <div class="callout__content">
    <p><strong>Ready?</strong> Once you've completed the checklist, you're all set. Head to <strong>Unit 1: Socrates and Plato</strong> to begin the course!</p>
  </div>
</div>
